<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osnabrück</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osnabrück is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the Hase river. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> founded a bishopric there around 780, and its prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> ruled a territory in north-west Germany until 1803. Together with Münster it hosted the negotiations of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a>, which ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a> in 1648.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osnabruck.jpg" alt="Osnabrück" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: El Grafo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osnabr%C3%BCck_aerial.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
